    "reading": "TY2023: the three-or-more cell at $30,000 to $35,000 prints a numeric 0 with no disclosure marker. The child blocks exceed the all-returns columns by 310,212 returns at $25,000 to $30,000 and by 1,187 at $20,000 to $25,000, and fall 311,398 returns ($1,724,074 thousand) short at $30,000 to $35,000; the three residuals sum to 1 return. Subtracting each residual from the three-or-more column gives a smooth column, while the other child columns already run smoothly. The likeliest reading is that IRS placed the $30,000 to $35,000 cell's returns and amount in the $25,000 to $30,000 row (and a few in the $20,000 to $25,000 row). IRS has not confirmed this. TY2021 shows the same pattern in the one-child column ($45,000 to $50,000 prints 0; its returns sit in the $25,000 to $30,000 row); TY2022 shows none.",
